Compunet Reborn - Amiga Client v{VERSION}
=========================================

A native Amiga client for the Compunet Reborn online service - the recovered 1989
Amiga Compunet client, reconstructed and re-pointed at the Reborn server over TCP/IP.

WHAT IS COMPUNET?
  Compunet (aka CNet) was a UK interactive online service that ran from 1984
  to 1993, serving the Commodore 64 community. It offered user-generated content,
  electronic mail ("Courier"), telesoftware downloads, a page editor, multi-user
  Partyline chat, and the iconic horizontally-scrolling "duckshoot" menu.
  Compunet Reborn brings it back to life over the modern internet.

REGISTRATION (required)
  You need a (free) Compunet Reborn account to log in. Register on the website:

      https://compunet.live/

REQUIREMENTS
  * An Amiga running Workbench / Kickstart 2.1 or higher.
  * A TCP/IP stack that provides bsdsocket.library (AmiTCP, Roadshow, Miami, ...),
    installed and online.

SETUP
  * Edit the "TCPHOST" file to point at the server. Format:  host  or  host:port
    (default port {PORT}). The shipped default is:  {HOST}
  * Make sure your TCP/IP stack is up, then double-click the Compunet icon.

CONTENTS
  Compunet            the client
  CnetEditor          frame / page editor (launched from the client)
  CnetTty             interactive terminal viewer (Partyline, live sessions)
  cnet-configuration  saved settings (phone/user fields; edit in-client via Setup)
  TCPHOST             server address

Compunet Reborn:  https://compunet.live/
